2026-11-10T11:35:50.2734406Z    image gate: house_1918_prairie chicagology_photo: verdict "differs", 5 difference(s) open: the belvedere's corner pilasters and the columns of its arched frames (x 1530-1560 and 1690-1744 px; x 1565-1645): the kit's pilasters run the whole height of a bay, so the belvedere's alone are not built; the window dressings: the photograph's pedimented and scrolled brownstone hoods, the paired principal windows and the round-headed chamber lights on the south flank; built as K09's corniced lintels over flat-headed sashes; the south side east of the dining range (T-3370, seen through the re-solved camera): the photograph's face between the dining range's dark east return (x 1125-1170 px) and the south-east corner (x 1425) runs full height to the main cornice with a pair of windows to each storey (x 1220-1315 px); the build has the reception room's half-octagonal bay there, two storeys under its own low roof, standing before a wall the cornice crosses higher up; the deck's south-east corner (T-3370, fourth pass): the print's rail turns its south-east corner at x 1345 px, y 257; the build's turns at about x 1377, y 253, so the railed deck stands about 1 m further east along the south side than the print's (or, the camera being single, about 1 m further north); the hip's level cut sets the deck's rectangle, and moving its east edge alone is not yet a K01 hip deck's parameter; the dining range's south face's length (T-3370, third pass): through the re-solved camera the photograph's face runs from x 833 px to its dark east return at x 1125-1170, about 10.4 m, where the build's (the 1911 sheet's u 0-9.03) ends at x 1084 with its return to 1129; so the return, and the wall east of it, stand about 40 px (1.3 m) west of the print's, and the windows on the face, placed at the print's fractions of it, 7-30 px west of the print's. Either the range is longer than the sheet draws it or the camera's depth along the flank is off (its RESIDUAL TENSION at the south-east corner is the same sense); not settled here
